#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125385} :activity/id #uuid "e7c42f54-2ba5-576a-b2e1-2db695e51ec2" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125385 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125778 :tutorial/content "We already learned that the rank of a matrix $A$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ Now, can we obtain any information from the *non-pivot* columns?\n\nThe answer is yes! The non-pivot columns help to find the dimension of the null space of a matrix $A,$ and here's how.\n\nConsider the matrix \n![](images/99/991b6f0c69e6341620139db9bfce5303785be21760eb8d630bfee92c57d4bc6a.svg)\n\nThe matrix $A$ is already in row echelon form, where the $1$st and the $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd one is a *non-pivot* column. Now, to get the null space of $A,$ we need to find the solution of the system\n\n![](images/1c/1cd56dc26ad4f478c3d7cb14375b8b2e45ef68e3215e79494d56108fecec39cb.svg)\n\nwhere $\\color{blue}x_1$ and ${\\color{blue}x_3}$ are basic variables and $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable. Hence, we obtain that \n\n![](images/56/56587dc5c1c98493060edb3561c13aa1576187461418619684459dd1f55626fe.svg)\n\nis a basis of $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))={\\color{red}1}$.\n\nIn other words,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is equal to the number of *non-pivot* columns in the corresponding row echelon form of $A$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$  is the number of *free variables* in the corresponding homogeneous system with the coefficient matrix $A.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7c75fc81-c464-5eea-bb66-37258ca64cb5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3520 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8764d6f6-efe5-555a-9b58-2ea9897c7843" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125386}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125386 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124508 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99"} :step/id #uuid "1781ce33-0951-5cf7-ba14-893c43247e6f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125387}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125387 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72"} :step/id #uuid "32808740-b993-5939-9a08-6bc3eab6463c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125388}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125388 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125779 :tutorial/content "The dimension of the null space of a matrix $A$ is often called the **nullity** of $A$. We will also use the following notation:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)).\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e46fe003-9e24-5794-b139-5c2805d463c5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3521 :tutorial/title "The Nullity of a Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "966d2e1c-4409-5d1b-996d-fad6a9c4d98c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125389}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125389 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124510 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b"} :step/id #uuid "0b0649dd-72fb-5d4a-a416-f1ca94874689"}] :activity/title "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124684} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436690} :activity/id #uuid "1e33c8a4-5627-57c9-a7ac-4e77bb151165" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321072 :question/id #uuid "da3efbc4-2fa4-54a8-9aa9-e1c2c723490a"} :step/id #uuid "034d01d2-7fd8-5b65-910e-ac88f27f255e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436687}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436687 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124876 :question/id #uuid "6a0b3d6d-593b-5e4e-ba8b-3eae5b6b11d4"} :step/id #uuid "4760dd1d-3298-58a3-b976-41ff6b4b2fae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436689}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436688 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436685 :question/id #uuid "e39062c0-8f9b-52cc-adaa-1df745d5f896"} :step/id #uuid "5674bd5f-5ced-5ae8-83dc-206575be79e5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436689 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17