times 6$ matrix that has $4$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(P))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $P.$ \n\nSince $P$ has $6$ columns and $4$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $P$ is \n\n$$\n6-4=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(P))=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7299ad-6dd4-5e36-a960-baad7b2dfd99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446019} {:answer/id #uuid "72c58192-a657-55f8-9c75-3a730310340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446027} {:answer/id #uuid "922c6d6a-9084-59f6-8242-39f020ceb426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446029} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7b8c7e-f012-5c38-b09b-7e31cf2fb4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446031} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e70dfe-da3a-5ba2-b04b-e32f3540f68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446039} :answer-field/id #uuid "db681804-d5a4-581f-a070-ccb28a60d3f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446045}] :question/id #uuid "28cc22ad-5eb3-5579-a4be-2d8af449af5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79337" :question/problem "Let $S$ be a $9\\times 12$ matrix that has $7$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $S?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(S))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $S.$ \n\nSince $S$ has $12$ columns and $7$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $S$ is \n\n$$\n12-7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(S))=5.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124318 :question/id #uuid "4aa47a89-9f9b-55d8-ba01-a131b20e6c95" :question/math-academy-id "e-5421" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If ![](images/77/77c0dd8d9b925b3310c5470f272b59e2b9d25bb141295741f1748771b6c454c1.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\nII. If ![](images/86/86c4f440750b5d7bf45e8c36b6fd9852c2749ac56331b3e0d76a6901acaf5b60.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\nIII. If ![](images/22/2295be7f70c3de36b51784b2919af95695f5520abdb2300287a17852b4cbfce3.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc909b1-8785-5945-9459-d053d2c7079c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459835} {:answer/id #uuid "52c418de-d88b-5235-9bf5-be2556fb9846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459836} :answer-field/id #uuid "55564640-7655-5d3c-bf63-8297180991a2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169e939e-6301-511d-8c0c-090a2f18ccdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459837} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd9e1cc-c00a-5419-a142-d9bc5d4f5345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459837} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca7871e-e659-5912-aa33-fc7d1986742f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97736f06-c485-5e15-91c2-2eba3c226429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459839} {:answer/id #uuid "0670e564-4f2a-597b-bb60-ec48ef5ea2c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459840} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a13967f-4100-5e9e-a96a-a678a0efc380" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460786}] :question/id #uuid "5f568aea-24ab-542a-9112-9bb117e4fc0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34904" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n- **II.** If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- **III.** If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa598fb-5b9e-5eab-8d75-ba9506c4ca84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319419} {:answer/id #uuid "22844e7a-ef6b-57a6-8284-3bbb51cbd945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319498} {:answer/id #uuid "9b20d76c-e6ca-5977-8498-bd058294bd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319857} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d88661-d88d-54c8-9c09-88200cbc595f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320008} {:answer/id #uuid "d82e6665-8a18-5233-bacf-3d6116645e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320051} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a491e9-6bdb-50a9-8234-00b00fcda03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320365}] :question/id #uuid "1eb36ea9-01c5-5b94-89ae-678eeae6fd31" :question/math-academy-id "q-35349" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1+2+0=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "883ff5fb-cd92-5295-9749-a73ce52161a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449538} {:answer/id #uuid "2e88af28-4c09-5fdd-833e-3651c7b725a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449538} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce0ae24-e14f-528f-9ca2-cb88c8ee5075" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37eb73c9-f986-55cc-9e3f-f09e85663a40" :answer/ty