s and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144c29d5-259f-5f89-8bab-62bb199092ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269447} {:answer/id #uuid "7de0c11c-f9e7-5ad9-98a4-df940f432748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270371} {:answer/id #uuid "a0cc509d-af1c-5448-919b-9887e4870a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270696} {:answer/id #uuid "af9b7d7a-0f84-5e91-b602-24d8c6ceb11e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270831} {:answer/id #uuid "ef529106-3dcb-5606-95ff-1a84feece20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270696} :answer-field/id #uuid "19abb6c3-f597-5f9c-976e-d96871063ea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271555}] :question/id #uuid "b261a1e5-ed3a-59cd-ae99-4580be4ac004" :question/math-academy-id "q-139974" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd  column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2+1+1=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0064e2-7095-50a4-9f68-f09ccda97572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450548} {:answer/id #uuid "87590c0b-b8a7-56c3-9915-4df9e724e9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549} :answer-field/id #uuid "71819ef2-7ff5-5f57-beb5-0822cdadf30b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a417e97-6614-5b7a-935f-3f703efe4728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450550} {:answer/id #uuid "705d803b-01fe-5cbc-9e39-520b711450ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4d11a6