s \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e278eb04-9ea2-5844-b05e-b7780ac79ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450554} {:answer/id #uuid "9c39f12c-2213-5317-b25b-2b94303ac001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555} :answer-field/id #uuid "2574fec4-c774-5e83-88c2-54c6e3934238" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e20627b5-0399-56be-bf11-b108f477de32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} {:answer/id #uuid "fd76fc07-6256-5abb-ada4-e6122e1a413e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b81185-37e8-5204-a76c-9cca612b39b1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b008e94-bd7d-587f-b70b-14f6d36a4468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a6b4d9-1c23-50e1-93df-86fd6c5da0a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da1ea97-6d5c-56ad-aad8-3bac4d1c60b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451233}] :question/id #uuid "56ebc46d-299b-5fda-a402-a93bacc04806" :question/math-academy-id "q-34973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\n- **II.** If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\n- **III.** If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3481e207-e3b3-5e18-a809-b68d786d6e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319553} {:answer/id #uuid "49662fce-308a-5973-9daf-90f661164bb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319609} {:answer/id #uuid "85f18eb3-e6ce-502e-be45-f3e00050dbb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319794} {:answer/id #uuid "b176021e-5d4f-5d30-bf8d-ae821e8d1a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319934} {:answer/id #uuid "ca6939af-8bae-5b13-92b7-db8af3689ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319609} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c4879d1-521b-5d88-bd53-72f2ed650b99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320450}] :question/id #uuid "da3efbc4-2fa4-54a8-9aa9-e1c2c723490a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35316" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425382} {:answer/id #uuid "62c579bb-353a-5222-8c49-b704acbe87e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425387} {:answer/id #